+## Profile memory policy
+
+```yaml
+mcp:
+  memory_saving: true
+```
+
+`mcp.memory_saving` defaults to `false`. When enabled, configured stdio servers
+with a valid schema cache default to lazy startup: tool schemas are available
+before their processes start. The first tool call opens the server. New, changed
+or expired cache entries still require live discovery.
+
+Explicit per-server `lazy` values win, including `false`. HTTP servers and servers
+with `events: true` keep their existing policy. Portable stdio definitions merged
+into the profile use the same default. Direct session-owned/programmatic server
+definitions are unaffected. The setting applies on subsequent discovery/startup;
+it does not stop already-connected servers or rewrite their configuration.
+
+`memory_saving` alone does not set an idle timeout. To also retire restart-safe
+stdio servers after use, opt in separately:
+
+```yaml
+mcp:
+  memory_saving: true
+  idle_timeout_seconds: 5
+```
+
+`mcp.idle_timeout_seconds` defaults to `0.0` (disabled). Positive finite seconds
+(including numeric strings) supply a default to stdio servers without events;
+HTTP and event-enabled servers receive no inherited timeout. Invalid, boolean,
+nonfinite, zero and negative global values leave server policies unchanged.
+The idle option works independently of `memory_saving` and applies after portable
+definitions merge. Neither setting rewrites the configuration file.
+
+The presence of a server `idle_timeout_seconds` key, either at the top level or
+inside `lifecycle:`, prevents inheritance, even for `0`, `null` or invalid values.
